%% Authlane OAuth 2.0 + PKCE Flow
%% Render with: https://mermaid.live

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant User as End User
    participant SaaS as SaaS Application
    participant Authlane as Authlane API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant OAuth as OAuth Provider<br/>(GitHub, Slack, etc.)

    Note over User,OAuth: Phase 1: Initiate OAuth Flow

    User->>SaaS: Click "Connect GitHub"
    SaaS->>Authlane: GET /api/v1/users/{userId}/connections/github/authorize

    Note over Authlane: Generate PKCE pair:<br/>code_verifier (random 32 bytes)<br/>code_challenge = SHA256(code_verifier)

    Note over Authlane: Generate state token<br/>(random 32 bytes)

    Authlane->>DB: INSERT connection<br/>(status='pending', metadata={state, pkce})
    DB-->>Authlane: Connection created

    Authlane-->>SaaS: { authorizationUrl: "https://github.com/login/oauth/authorize?..." }
    SaaS->>User: Redirect to OAuth provider

    Note over User,OAuth: Phase 2: User Authorization

    User->>OAuth: Authenticate with provider
    OAuth->>User: Show authorization prompt
    User->>OAuth: Approve access
    OAuth-->>User: Redirect to callback URL<br/>?code=xxx&state=yyy

    Note over User,OAuth: Phase 3: Token Exchange

    User->>Authlane: GET /callback?code=xxx&state=yyy

    Authlane->>DB: SELECT connection WHERE metadata.state = 'yyy'
    DB-->>Authlane: Connection (with PKCE verifier)

    alt State mismatch or not found
        Authlane-->>User: Error: Invalid state (CSRF protection)
    end

    Authlane->>OAuth: POST /oauth/token<br/>{code, code_verifier, client_id, client_secret}

    alt Invalid code or PKCE
        OAuth-->>Authlane: Error: invalid_grant
        Authlane->>DB: UPDATE connection SET status='error'
        Authlane-->>User: Error: OAuth failed
    end

    OAuth-->>Authlane: {access_token, refresh_token, expires_in}

    Note over Authlane: Encrypt tokens with AES-256-GCM

    Authlane->>DB: UPDATE connection<br/>SET credentials_enc=..., status='connected'

    Note over Authlane,DB: Phase 4: Schedule Token Refresh (if Redis available)

    opt Refresh token present
        Authlane->>Redis: Schedule refresh job<br/>at (expires_at - 5 min)
    end

    Authlane-->>User: Redirect to success URL

    Note over User,OAuth: Phase 5: Use Credentials

    SaaS->>Authlane: GET /api/v1/users/{userId}/connections/github/credentials

    Authlane->>DB: SELECT credentials_enc FROM connections
    DB-->>Authlane: Encrypted credentials

    Note over Authlane: Decrypt with AES-256-GCM

    alt Token expired
        Note over Authlane: Attempt refresh
        Authlane->>OAuth: POST /oauth/token (refresh_token)
        OAuth-->>Authlane: New tokens
        Authlane->>DB: UPDATE credentials
    end

    Authlane-->>SaaS: { access_token, token_type, expires_at }
    SaaS->>OAuth: API call with access_token
    OAuth-->>SaaS: API response
